From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Actually enable ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL (it was wired to nothing)

WHY IS HUNSPELL STILL LINKED?

Not because a flag misbehaved -- because upstream built the entire strip
mechanism and then never connected the switch to it.

`ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL` is consulted in six places, all of them complete
and correct:

  Repository.mk:376                          -- drops the hyphen/lnth/spell
                                                library registrations
  RepositoryExternal.mk:573                  -- drops gb_LinkTarget__use_hunspell
                                                and gb_ExternalProject__use_hunspell
  lingucomponent/Module_lingucomponent.mk:19 -- drops Library_hyphen, Library_lnth,
                                                Library_spell, StaticLibrary_ulingu
  external/hunspell/StaticLibrary_hunspell.mk:23 -- drops hunspell.cxx
  external/hyphen/ExternalProject_hyphen.mk:12   -- drops the hunspell dependency
  external/mythes/ExternalProject_mythes.mk:12   -- drops the hunspell dependency

And the variable itself is hardcoded to the empty string:

  config_host.mk.in:259  export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL=

configure.ac never assigns it and never AC_SUBSTs it; the only mention there is
line 3375, `#    AC_DEFINE(ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL)`, commented out. So
`ifneq ($(ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL),TRUE)` is true in every build that has
ever been made, and all six guards are dead code. The neighbouring
ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_GUESSLANG (line 258) shows what the line was meant to say.

This is why --without-fonts and --disable-gui had no effect on it: hunspell is
not reached through either. It is reached because libspelllo.a / libhyphenlo.a /
liblnthlo.a each declare a .component file, and solenv/gbuild/static.mk:66-67
force-links EVERY library that has one into the static `components` library:

    $(foreach lib,$(gb_Library_KNOWNLIBS),$(if $(call gb_Library__get_component,$(lib)), \
        $(eval $(call gb_Library_use_libraries,components,$(lib)))))

`components` is then linked into soffice_bin with -Wl,--whole-archive
(desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk), and solenv/bin/native-code.py emits a
static map naming lingucomponent_SpellChecker/Hyphenator/Thesaurus_get_implementation
by symbol, so --gc-sections can never reach them. Feature flags are not part of
that decision at any point.

WHY IT IS SAFE

The three services are already inert at runtime in this build. No dictionaries
ship: the `dictionaries` module is not in BUILD_TYPE, there is not a single
.aff/.dic/.dat hyphenation or spelling dictionary in instdir, and the runtime
VFS (soffice.data) holds 86 files, none of them dictionary data. So
SpellChecker/Hyphenator/Thesaurus register with zero locales today, and every
consumer already takes the "no service" branch:

  - sw/source/core/text/inftxt.cxx:1743-1763 SwTextFormatInfo::IsHyphenate()
    returns false when xHyph->hasLocale() is false, which it already is. Line
    breaking is unchanged, so PDF pagination is unchanged.
  - linguistic/source/hyphdsp.cxx:283-287 returns nullptr (not throw) when no
    service is registered for the locale; likewise createPossibleHyphens() and
    queryAlternativeSpelling().
  - editeng/source/misc/unolingu.cxx:483-533 LinguMgr::GetHyphenator() never
    returns null -- it falls back to HyphDummy_Impl -- so the two unguarded
    call sites (sw/source/core/text/guess.cxx:893, sw/source/core/edit/
    acorrect.cxx:553) stay safe.
  - linguistic/source/spelldsp.cxx:261 isValid_Impl() returns "word is fine".
  - linguistic/source/lngsvcmgr.cxx:931-946 GetAvailableSpellSvcs_Impl() and
    its siblings emplace an empty vector before enumerating, so an empty
    component map is the handled case, not an edge case.

Nothing throws; the sites that could complain use SAL_WARN or debug-only
DBG_ASSERT/OSL_ENSURE.

Document IMPORT never touches linguistics at all: grepping sw/source/filter/,
sw/source/writerfilter/ and oox/ for LinguMgr|XSpellChecker|XHyphenator|
XThesaurus returns nothing. Spell checking is reached only via SwLayIdle
(sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx:2245), gated on IsOnlineSpell().

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY KEPT

  - `linguistic` (liblnglo.a, 201.8 KiB of retained code). This is the
    null-object layer -- LngSvcMgr, SpellCheckerDispatcher, HyphenatorDispatcher,
    DicList -- that makes all of the graceful degradation above work. Removing
    it is NOT covered by this patch and is not safe.
  - `numbertext` (libnumbertextlo.a). NumberText lives in its own library and
    Module_lingucomponent.mk:36-39 adds it OUTSIDE every guard, so this patch
    does not touch it. It is genuinely live during conversion:
    i18npool/source/nativenumber/nativenumbersupplier.cxx:605-623 uses it for
    NatNum12 number formatting.

PRECEDENT

ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_GUESSLANG is already TRUE in this build and the identical
removal worked: lingucomponent_LangGuess_get_implementation is absent from the
generated services_constructors.list even though native-code.py:311 hardcodes
it, and libguesslanglo.a is absent from services.rdb. Nothing regressed.

MEASURED SAVING

Retained code attributed to libspelllo.a + libhyphenlo.a + liblnthlo.a +
libhunspell-1.7.a in the linked pre-wasm-opt soffice.wasm, by intersecting the
binary's name section against each archive's WASM_SYMBOL_TABLE:

    159 functions, 121,128 bytes exclusive (118.3 KiB)
    largest: SpellChecker::GetSpellFailure 52,892 B
             Thesaurus::queryMeanings      10,457 B
             Hyphenator::hyphenate          5,362 B

Plus hunspell's data tables: 399.7 KiB of data segments exist in
libhunspell-1.7.a; scaling by the measured 27% code-retention ratio gives
~100-110 KiB actually retained (ESTIMATE, not measured -- data segments cannot
be attributed to an archive from the linked binary).

Wire estimate ~55-75 KiB brotli, using the module's own raw->wire factor of
0.202 (117,190,355 B linked -> 95,893,393 B after wasm-opt -> 23,700,411 B
brotli) for the code and a worse ratio for the data tables.

RISK / WHAT WOULD BREAK

If a document requests automatic hyphenation, its line breaks would change --
but only if a hyphenation dictionary were present, and none is, so this is a
no-op today. If dictionaries are ever added to the VFS, this patch must be
reverted first. The hyphenation layout tests already self-skip on
`!xHyphenator->hasLocale(en-US)` (sw/qa/extras/layout/layout2.cxx:1218), which
is direct evidence the services are already inert.

Test that would catch a regression: `./tests/run_validation.sh --visual`
(pixel-level PDF comparison) on a DOCX with automatic hyphenation enabled, plus
`./tests/run_validation.sh --text`. The build-integration guard is that the
services_constructors.list is regenerated from the built .component files, so a
stale reference is impossible.

diff --git a/config_host.mk.in b/config_host.mk.in
--- a/config_host.mk.in
+++ b/config_host.mk.in
@@ -256,7 +256,10 @@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_EPUB=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_EXTRA=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_GUESSLANG=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
-export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL=
+# WASM: was hardcoded empty, which made all six ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL
+# guards in the tree dead code. A headless converter never spell-checks and
+# this build ships no dictionaries, so follow GUESSLANG above.
+export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_HUNSPELL=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_LANGUAGETOOL=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_LOCALES=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
 export ENABLE_WASM_STRIP_PINGUSER=@ENABLE_WASM_STRIP@
